From: IBM United Kingdom Ltd <legal@ibm-uk.example> (IBM United Kingdom)
To: CIS General Insurance Ltd <legal@cisgil.example> (CIS General Insurance)
Date: 2017-06-22
Subject: Final Notice under clause 26.7 of the MSA - invoice 5803171298

We refer to our invoice dated 24 March 2017 in the sum of £2,889,600, invoice number: 5803171298 (the "Invoice"). Pursuant to paragraph 11.7 of Schedule 5 of the MSA, the Invoice was due and payable by 4 April 2017. To date we have not yet received payment. It is now over 45 days since the Invoice was due and payable. As such we hereby give you notice that if the Invoice is not paid within the next 15 Business Days we intend to terminate the MSA as per clause 26.7 of the MSA. IBM reserves all of its rights in full.

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: CIS General Insurance v IBM [2021] EWHC 347 (TCC), paras 13, 176.
